{
  "_comment": [
    "Benchmark registry. Every row was verified against the live Hugging Face API on 2026-07-28.",
    "The `eval_split` field is the one that matters and the one most tools get wrong: for",
    "HellaSwag, PIQA, WinoGrande and CommonsenseQA the `test` split exists but its labels are",
    "blanked, so scoring happens on `validation`. IFEval's only split is `train` and it IS the",
    "eval set. GPQA is gated and has no test split at all.",
    "`license` is null where the Hub repo carries no license tag. We do not substitute the",
    "license from the original paper, because that would be a guess presented as a fact.",
    "`shippable` marks whether we prebuild and distribute a hashed 8-gram index for it."
  ],
